# 0.1.19: let go in the wheel's middle (a tester on 0.1.18: "you cant go back to fist with your right hand once you use a
# gun. Maybe just releasing in the middle of the weapon wheel should go back to fists?"). Akimbo (the default), Wheel pick
# on Point (the default), eight weapons (QUEST_SIM_GIVE), the Blaster in the right hand (QUEST_SIM_HOLD=15) and the
# Pyrocitor in the left (QUEST_SIM_LEFT=16), on Novalis.
# The right hand's wheel: the dot to its middle (between wheelpoint.sim's icons: yaw -11.5, pitch 3.2), rested there and
# let go: "[vr-ring] let go in the wheel's middle: the right hand's item 15 put away, the hand empty", the wrench on the
# grip and put down. The trigger then: "[vr-wrench] the trigger asks the last gun back", the Blaster out again.
# A quick pass, on the wheel's second page (the trigger turns it, as in wheelpoint.sim; the first page's slots are empty
# here): the dot on the lower right icon a moment (slot 3, item 11: Swap at full speed takes it; the right icon,
# slot 2, is the Pyrocitor the left hand holds, greyed for this hand), then to the middle and let go at once: nothing put
# away, the hand keeps that weapon.
# The left hand's wheel (wheelleft.sim's mirror, yaw 11.5): rested in its middle and let go: "[vr-ring] let go in the
# wheel's middle: the left hand's gun put away, the hand empty".
